{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01310",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.1,
      "end_seconds": 7.2,
      "duration_seconds": 6.1,
      "text": "Doctor, this one's ready for you. Everything's on the chart, but I'll go through it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.81,
      "end_seconds": 11.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "Thank you. Right, hello, what's the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 17.38,
      "end_seconds": 27.07,
      "duration_seconds": 9.69,
      "text": "Yeah, it's watery diarrhoea, mostly. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 28.03,
      "end_seconds": 38.51,
      "duration_seconds": 10.48,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Temperature is 39.1 degrees, blood pressure 120 over 74, heart rate 102, respiratory rate 17."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.21,
      "end_seconds": 41.62,
      "duration_seconds": 1.41,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.19,
      "end_seconds": 62.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.63,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.39,
      "end_seconds": 69.14,
      "duration_seconds": 4.75,
      "text": "Mostly mild. Only oral rehydration, and it's not much."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.28,
      "end_seconds": 73.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "What about crampy tummy pain, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.66,
      "end_seconds": 80.58,
      "duration_seconds": 5.92,
      "text": "Yes, about the same, ten days. Right, I've been feeling sick too."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.94,
      "end_seconds": 86.96,
      "duration_seconds": 5.02,
      "text": "And what about blood in the stool, severe dehydration or vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.23,
      "end_seconds": 94.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "Let me think, no, none that I've noticed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.41,
      "end_seconds": 98.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "Anything different when you pass water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.1,
      "end_seconds": 101.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "No, that's all fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.43,
      "end_seconds": 105.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "Any problems with your joints or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 106.46,
      "end_seconds": 108.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "I move fine otherwise."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.29,
      "end_seconds": 111.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "What about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 112.24,
      "end_seconds": 119.8,
      "duration_seconds": 7.56,
      "text": "I've, I've got an irregular heartbeat. I, I have high blood pressure. Yes, gout."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.71,
      "end_seconds": 131.58,
      "duration_seconds": 10.87,
      "text": "I see, go ahead. Right, so an irregular heartbeat and gout are already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.89,
      "end_seconds": 143.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "Let's run through your medicines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.96,
      "end_seconds": 149.95,
      "duration_seconds": 4.99,
      "text": "Yeah, I take apixaban, 5 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 150.49,
      "end_seconds": 155.57,
      "duration_seconds": 5.08,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 2.5 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 156.78,
      "end_seconds": 159.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "Alright. Did you bring the up-to-date prescription?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.39,
      "end_seconds": 178.03,
      "duration_seconds": 16.64,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time. Allopurinol, 100 milligrams, once a day. Oral rehydration salts. I take it 1 sachet, after each loose stool. Lisinopril I don't take anymore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.69,
      "end_seconds": 180.44,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "Who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.06,
      "end_seconds": 184.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.29,
      "end_seconds": 188.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "Tell me about your eating."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 190.11,
      "end_seconds": 196.35,
      "duration_seconds": 6.24,
      "text": "I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 198.43,
      "end_seconds": 203.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.72,
      "text": "Alright, do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 205.03,
      "end_seconds": 207.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Yes, I'm allergic to amoxicillin."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.77,
      "end_seconds": 212.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Let's move on to the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.7,
      "end_seconds": 215.11,
      "duration_seconds": 1.41,
      "text": "Nearly finished here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.86,
      "end_seconds": 230.63,
      "duration_seconds": 6.77,
      "text": "Your tummy is soft with mild general tenderness and your mouth is a little dry."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.37,
      "end_seconds": 236.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "Thank you, you can get dressed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.82,
      "end_seconds": 262.18,
      "duration_seconds": 8.36,
      "text": "Let me tell you where I've got to. This looks most like travellers' diarrhoea. We shouldn't forget a parasitic infection."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 264.16,
      "end_seconds": 267.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "What are the odds it's serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.63,
      "end_seconds": 297.46,
      "duration_seconds": 24.83,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's travellers' diarrhoea, and we'll know more once the a stool sample is back. We should do a stool sample for diarrhoea after travel. Drink plenty of fluids and wash your hands carefully. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 299.48,
      "end_seconds": 301.0,
      "duration_seconds": 1.52,
      "text": "Alright, I follow."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.64,
      "end_seconds": 314.95,
      "duration_seconds": 12.31,
      "text": "If the symptoms get worse, or you feel really unwell, please come to the emergency department. Come back if it lasts more than a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 316.02,
      "end_seconds": 320.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "Mm, I'll book it on my way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 324.95,
      "end_seconds": 328.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 329.45,
      "end_seconds": 331.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "Thank you, doctor, goodbye."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 332.57,
      "end_seconds": 333.82,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "Look after yourself."
    }
  ]
}